## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests analyzed · 7 Critical · 1 High · 1 Medium · 1 Low**

This suite is the textbook example of **coverage-touching**: every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (giving ~95% coverage), but almost nothing is verified. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**, and the remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` — which merely confirms the method returned *something*, not the *right* thing.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic — all 10 tests)

The suite methodically walks every public method in declaration order (`AddProduct`, `GetProduct`, `UpdatePrice`, …, `ImportFromCsv`) with no meaningful verification. This is not testing — it is **coverage theater**.

#### 2. No Assertions (6 tests)

| Test (line) | What it calls | What it asserts |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | `AddProduct` | **nothing** |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (33) | `UpdatePrice` | **nothing** |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (39) | `RemoveProduct` | **nothing** |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (64) | `GetProductCount` | **nothing** |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (69) | `ApplyBulkDiscount` | **nothing** |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (85) | `ImportFromCsv` | **nothing** |

**Fix** (example for `AddProduct_Works`):
```csharp
// BEFORE
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

**Fix** (example for `UpdatePrice_Works`):
```csharp
// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

**Fix** (example for `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`):
```csharp
// AFTER — verify the 10% discount was applied
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 10.00m));
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var discounted = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(9.00m, discounted?.Price);
```

#### 3. Weak `IsNotNull` Assertions (3 tests)

